IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`
IMPORT `bnra-part3`

-- Tests for Part 3 (ss 32 to 45).  Figures read off the text: fines of $1,000, $5,000 and
-- $10,000 and terms of 12 and 24 months (ss 11(12), 22(3), 32(4), 34(1), 35, 43(3), 45(5)(b));
-- composition up to the lower of one half of the maximum fine and $5,000 (s 37); 14 days to make
-- good (s 39); deemed service one day after ordinary delivery and 2 days after registered posting
-- (s 42(2)); 3 January 2016 and 30 days (s 45).

§ `Tests -- Part 3`

§§ `32. Inspection`

-- Inspection Facts: authorised in writing, employee of the Authority or a public officer, reason to believe a person carries on
-- business at the premises, declared office, produced written authority, person fails to comply or obstructs.
`a properly authorised inspector` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an inspector authorised orally` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an inspector who is neither employee nor public officer` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an inspector with no reason to believe` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an obstructed inspector who declared office and showed authority` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`an obstructed inspector who did not declare office` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`an obstructed inspector who did not produce written authority` MEANS `Inspection Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the person is validly authorised as an inspector` `a properly authorised inspector`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is validly authorised as an inspector` `an inspector authorised orally`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is validly authorised as an inspector` `an inspector who is neither employee nor public officer`
#ASSERT `the Registrar or an inspector may enter the premises` `a properly authorised inspector`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar or an inspector may enter the premises` `an inspector with no reason to believe`
#ASSERT `the Registrar or inspector has complied with section 32(3)` `a properly authorised inspector`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar or inspector has complied with section 32(3)` `an obstructed inspector who did not declare office`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar or inspector has complied with section 32(3)` `an obstructed inspector who did not produce written authority`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 32(4)` `an obstructed inspector who declared office and showed authority`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 32(4)` `an obstructed inspector who did not declare office`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 32(4)` `an obstructed inspector who did not produce written authority`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 32(4)` `a properly authorised inspector`

§§ `33. Power of Registrar to obtain further information`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may require the person to answer in writing or summon the person to answer orally` (`Information Request Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may require the person to answer in writing or summon the person to answer orally` (`Information Request Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `34. Restriction on undischarged bankrupt carrying on business`

-- Bankrupt Facts: undischarged bankrupt, carries on business required to be registered, takes part in the management of such a
-- business, High Court permission, Official Assignee's written permission, notice served on the Official Assignee who was heard.
`a bankrupt running a registrable business without permission` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bankrupt managing someone else's registrable business without permission` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bankrupt with High Court permission` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`a bankrupt with the Official Assignee's written permission` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a discharged bankrupt running a registrable business` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bankrupt with no involvement in any registrable business` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bankrupt seeking permission after notice to the Official Assignee` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a bankrupt seeking permission without notice to the Official Assignee` MEANS `Bankrupt Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a bankrupt running a registrable business without permission`
#ASSERT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a bankrupt managing someone else's registrable business without permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a bankrupt with High Court permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a bankrupt with the Official Assignee's written permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a discharged bankrupt running a registrable business`
#ASSERT NOT `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` `a bankrupt with no involvement in any registrable business`
#ASSERT `the General Division of the High Court may give permission` `a bankrupt seeking permission after notice to the Official Assignee`
#ASSERT NOT `the General Division of the High Court may give permission` `a bankrupt seeking permission without notice to the Official Assignee`

§§ `35. Offences and penalties`

-- Offence Facts: required to be registered, carries on business unregistered, under a different name, after cancellation,
-- after cessation, fails to comply with a s 33 summons without lawful excuse, false statement, knows or has reason to believe
-- it false, not required in respect of the name under s 4.
`an unregistered trader` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a trader under a different name` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a trader after cancellation` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a trader after cessation` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unregistered trader who need not register for the name` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`an unregistered person who is not required to register` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a person who ignores a summons without excuse` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a person who gives false information knowingly` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a person who gives false information innocently` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a person with nothing wrong` MEANS `Offence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `an unregistered trader`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `a trader under a different name`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `a trader after cancellation`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `a trader after cessation`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `an unregistered trader who need not register for the name`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `an unregistered person who is not required to register`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` `a person with nothing wrong`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(b)` `a person who ignores a summons without excuse`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(b)` `a person with nothing wrong`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(c)` `a person who gives false information knowingly`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(c)` `a person who gives false information innocently`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(c)` `a person with nothing wrong`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(3)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(3)` FALSE

-- the maximum penalty for each offence provision
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to appoint an authorised representative or to lodge a notice (section 11(12))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 1_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to appoint an authorised representative or to lodge a notice (section 11(12))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to notify cessation of business (section 22(3))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to notify cessation of business (section 22(3))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to comply with a request of, or obstructing, the Registrar or an inspector (section 32(4))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to comply with a request of, or obstructing, the Registrar or an inspector (section 32(4))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an undischarged bankrupt carrying on or managing business (section 34(1))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `carrying on business unregistered, failing to comply with a summons, or a false statement (section 35(1))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `carrying on business unregistered, failing to comply with a summons, or a false statement (section 35(1))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to comply with section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3) (section 35(3))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to comply with section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3) (section 35(3))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `contravening regulations that so provide (section 43(3))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `contravening regulations that so provide (section 43(3))`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months, if imprisonment is available` EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `failing to appoint an authorised representative after commencement (section 45(5)(b))`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 1_000

§§ `36. Evidence of carrying on business under business name`

-- Display Facts: displayed in premises, evidence it refers to a business there, proof to the contrary.
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to be carrying on the business under that business name` (`Display Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed to be carrying on the business under that business name` (`Display Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
